190-For tests/builds/checks:
191:- prefer the smallest meaningful validation that matches the change
192-- when multiple validation routes exist, test the most risk-reducing path first
193-- if full test suite is unavailable or too expensive, run targeted checks and say what remains unverified
194-- do not claim integration safety from local syntax plausibility alone
195-- use bounded retry only for plausible transient failure
196:- prefer fallback or rollback over speculative patch widening
197-- if the plan or mutation path crosses an approval-sensitive zone, present the plan or patch shape for review before executing the broader action
