365-Plan approval rule:
--
422-Keep examples structural only.
423-Leave the codebase more correct, not merely more elaborate.
424:Keep lifecycle state and fallback route visible when the coding loop remains open.
425-When coding proof depends on stronger operational evidence, distinguish scenario definition, execution ledger, and release-facing proof strength explicitly.
426-Keep `scenario_id`, `run_id`, `cohort_id`, `trace_id`, and `artifact_version` stable when coding-proof, replay, and release artifacts remain linked.
427-Reject artifact joins that fail precedence, compatibility, freshness, or completeness checks; downgrade the claim rather than weakening executed proof.
